Remember the lowly jackal, that low-level critter only 
<barely> fit for human consumption?  Today I found a
wonderful new use for them .  .  .  .  .

POSSIBLE SPOILER ALERT


Whilst on my quest to please Morrigan enough to grant 
the blessed Stormbringer upon me I was embroiled in a 
savage fight with a jackalwere.  It bit me several times,
infecting me with lycanthropy.  No potions, no scrolls,
and unable to pray to Morrigan for several hundred turns.
Then I saw that as a werejackal I could summon my brethren
(other [mundane] jackals).  I quickly loped upstairs in
jackal form, entered the altar room, and summoned as many
times as I could before I returned to human form.  By that 
time I was able to pray to the goddess to remove the
lycanthropic taint.  I then calmly wielded Orcrist, the
two-handed sword of death, in anticipation of providing
many fresh corpses for sacrifice.   NOT!  I found that
all seven summoned jackals were my pets!  Imagine, seven
jackals jumping around your every step, eating all of
the corpses that you left behind, and sticking to your
side like glue so that you can't escape them by going to
a different level!  Chad13 (Cannabalistic Humanoid Above-
ground Dweller), resigned to his fate, went to the next
level followed by his faithful horde of jackals.  After
plodding into Kenicek's Armour Shoppe Chad went over to
a likely looking set of scale armor.  In poured the
happy-go-lucky jackal pack . . . and soon each jackal was
picking up a different set of armor . . . and each of
faithfully followed Chad out the door!  In a nearby room
Chad inspected his spoils:  cloak of invisibility, +2 
plate armor, and sundry bits of clothing.  Oh what fun
to rip Kenicek blind for some good items and then sell
the unused sets of armor back to the SOB.  Chad13 even
sold the same set of +0 black chainmail back to the
shopkeeper twice!  Happy   Happy   Happy!   Joy   Joy
   Joy!  Can't wait for the next shop, if the jackal
pack lives that long.  Thinking about naming them
after Santa's reindeer.  Appropriate, eh?

